These inputs are not tuning knobs; they are the research hypothesis written down. The enumerations define what a range is, what counts as a breakout, and what a unit of reward means. ENUM_BREAK_TRIGGER exists because traders genuinely disagree on whether a breakout needs a close beyond the boundary or merely a touch, so we measure it rather than assume it.
Four settings matter. InpServerOffsetHr keeps session presets consistent across brokers (GMT+2 vs GMT+3 changes the Tokyo range). InpBufferATR expresses tolerance in ATR multiples rather than points, so the same value behaves sensibly on other pairs. InpSuccessR and InpFailInsidePct define what winning means, and they are strict by design: a loose definition would flatter the strategy and teach us nothing.
