The session presets are applied and then shifted by the server offset before being wrapped back into a valid minute-of-day. The WrapMin helper performs a double modulo so that negative offsets behave correctly, which a single % operation in MQL5 would not guarantee. The window name is captured as a string at the same time and written into every row, so that files produced from different sessions can be concatenated later without losing track of where each event came from.
